ting review on behalf of Anglo American\n*Developed stakeholder management programs\nnterfaced regularly with local, state, national, and international media\n*Presented to/prepared regular briefings for Boards of Anglo American, Anglo Pebble, and\nPebble\nReported to/interfaced directly with London, Santiago, and Johannesburg offices\n+ Advanced Social Management Program Training (University of Cambridge / Queensland)\n\nResource Development Council, Anchorage, AK\nExecutive Director (2006-2011) Projects Coordinator AMEREF Executive Director (2000-2006)\n\u2018Researched and advocated for the responsible development of Alaska's natural resources\n*Coordinated meetings with, and attempted to achieve consensus from, diverse stakeholders\n*Developed delivered written and oral testimony to the legislature, governmental agencies,\nand public\n*State of Alaska registered lobbyist; Oversaw ballot measure campaigns\n+78-member Board management, development, and coordination\nSupervised staff and contractors including lobbyists and public affairs agencies\ntudget preparation and oversight\nCommunicated regularly with media outlets\n\nUniversity of Alaska Anchorage, Anchorage, AK\nAdjunct Professor-Web Site Development and MS Office\n\nUniversity of Alaska Anchorage, Anchorage, AK\nEnrollment Services, CAPP Coordinator|Curriculum and Publication Specialist\n\nNational Biological Service, Anchorage, AK\nPrince William Sound Primary Journal Research Assistant\n\nAlaska Pacific University, Anchorage, AK\nCollege Algebra Instructor and Graduate/Undergraduate Mathematics and Science Tutor",
